B. SMOTE&KM-SMOTE algorithm
To explore the impact of the data enhancement algorithm on our experiments, we conducted a set of comparative experiments using the SMOTE algorithm and the KM-SMOTE algorithm to examine the experimental results at different enhancement ratios.
Fig. 4 shows the changes in the recall and F1-score of the data enhancement ratio from 1.1 to 2 under the random forest method with only use Stylometric feature. We can see that the overall recall and F1-score are both decreasing after rising ﬁrst, and when the enhancement ratio comes to 1.8, we got the best results both SMOTE and KM-SMOTE algorithm. Compared to baseline results, our enhancement algorithm have better performance, which means enhancement algorithm have positive inﬂuence in detecting spear phishing emails and can generate new positive spear phishing instance.
From Fig. 4 we can also clearly get the conclusion that our improved KM-SMOTE algorithm have better enhancement performance, which indicate that the spear phishing emails in our dataset have different types and forms.
C. Comparison
After separately evaluating the impact of features and enhancement algorithms in detecting spear phishing emails, now we combined all the features and utilize KM-SMOTE algorithm with the enhancement ratio of 1.8 to examine our detecting performance using random forest.
