In 2017, Ho.,etc [5] made a brilliant work that with the dataset of 370 million emails where are only 19 spear phishing emails, they can successfully detect 17 spear phishing emails with only 0.005% false positive rate. The biggest difference between our work and Ho’s work is that their system built on complete and sufﬁcient LDAP, SMTP and NIDS logs, but our work don’t need the support of any historical record or any other logs. Many companies or organizations do not have the appropriate infrastructure to provide sufﬁcient logs or history records, so our work can be more adaptable and extensive.
VI. CONCLUSION In this paper, we focus on distinguishing spear phishing emails from phishing and benign emails. In order to solve the problems in previous research, we ﬁrst proposed forwarding and reputation features as our extended feature set, and we apply interpolation algorithm KM-SMOTE to reduce the impact of unbalanced data. Our data comes from the companies we cooperated with, containing 417 spear phishing emails and 13916 non-spear phishing emails. Finally, we were able to achieve a maximum recall of 95.56%, 98.85% of precision and 97.16% of F1-score in detecting spear phishing emails from phishing and benign emails. The results show that our proposed methods have great performance in detecting spear phishing emails, and our method don’t need the support of historical email record or other logs, which have more extensive adaptability than other exists method.
